  "key_findings": [
    "KV cache at 1M context: MHA FP16 requires 2560 GB vs MLA+TQ3 requires only 12.9 GB - a 199x reduction. Only MLA+TQ3 (12.9 GB) and GQA+TQ3 (60.0 GB) fit within H100 80GB HBM.",
    "GQA (FP16): compute/copy overlap hides 39.9% of I/O, achieving 1.67x speedup over sequential execution.",
    "MLA (FP16): compute/copy overlap hides 15.6% of I/O, achieving 1.19x speedup over sequential execution.",
    "GQA + TQ (3-bit): compute/copy overlap hides 11.4% of I/O, achieving 1.13x speedup over sequential execution.",
    "MLA + TQ (3-bit): compute/copy overlap hides 16.3% of I/O, achieving 1.20x speedup over sequential execution.",
    "I/O access patterns differ fundamentally: MHA reads 100% of KV cache contiguously, MLA reads only compressed latents (~7% of full dimensions), and TurboQuant DSA creates sparse discrete reads touching ~20-40% of addresses with 5.3x fewer bytes.",
    "MHA (FP16): TPOT=123.134ms, TTFT=72842.6ms, throughput=78 tok/s at batch=32.",
    "GQA (FP16): TPOT=17.805ms, TTFT=72842.6ms, throughput=106 tok/s at batch=32.",
    "MLA (FP16): TPOT=61.182ms, TTFT=54216.2ms, throughput=117 tok/s at batch=32.",
    "MHA + TQ (3-bit): TPOT=24.725ms, TTFT=72842.6ms, throughput=104 tok/s at batch=32.",
    "GQA + TQ (3-bit): TPOT=18.670ms, TTFT=72842.6ms, throughput=106 tok/s at batch=32.",
    "MLA + TQ (3-bit): TPOT=58.500ms, TTFT=54216.2ms, throughput=118 tok/s at batch=32."
  ],
